WEBVTT

00:11.636 --> 00:12.887
A KILLER PARADOX

00:12.971 --> 00:15.098
Stop right there. All right.

00:15.181 --> 00:16.558
-Now move this here.
-Okay.

00:16.641 --> 00:19.060
-We got a picture! Nice!
-We got a picture.

00:19.144 --> 00:21.104
-Hey!
-Oh, no.

00:21.187 --> 00:22.814
-Take this.
-Look at that!

00:22.897 --> 00:25.650
-Stretch out this part.
-Try to hold your palm flat.

00:26.985 --> 00:28.987
-No. Hold your palm flat.
-In you go!

00:29.863 --> 00:31.364
-Turn this.
-Okay!

00:31.448 --> 00:33.033
You having a good time there?

00:33.116 --> 00:36.911
-Perks of getting discharged.
-What are you talking about?

00:36.995 --> 00:38.872
I've been out six months already.

00:38.955 --> 00:40.999
Wow, really?

00:42.250 --> 00:44.210
Time flies when you're not doing anything.

00:45.754 --> 00:48.631
Yeong. Don't you have some work for Tang
while he's here?

00:48.715 --> 00:51.009
-Work? What?
-Oh, you know.

00:51.092 --> 00:52.594
Ah!

00:53.553 --> 00:54.554
SON SEONG-UK AND LEE YEONG

00:54.637 --> 00:56.306
I almost
didn't recognize the groom.

00:56.389 --> 00:58.641
He's your brother-in-law now.

00:58.725 --> 01:00.810
-Oh, right.
-Were you up all night gaming?

01:00.894 --> 01:03.480
I've been grinding.
You know I've been working.

01:03.563 --> 01:06.107
-My part-time job ends late.
-As if.

01:06.191 --> 01:08.860
Kid. I don't care if you're working
or playing games.

01:08.943 --> 01:11.404
-Go to bed when it's time to sleep.
-Yeah, yeah.

01:11.488 --> 01:12.697
How's the picture?

01:13.406 --> 01:15.283
Eh. It doesn't do you justice, honey.

01:15.366 --> 01:17.243
-Nah.
-I've only heard that from you.

01:17.327 --> 01:18.995
Oh, who was it? Jae-deok's son.

01:19.079 --> 01:22.040
-I heard he was tutoring or something.
-Oh, come on, Dad.

01:22.123 --> 01:25.877
-It's a few hours for decent money.
-University-wise, he's on another level.

01:25.960 --> 01:27.754
Think about it
from the parents' point of view.

01:27.837 --> 01:30.048
Would you want
your oldest son to be a tutor?

01:30.131 --> 01:31.883
Hah! That is true.

01:32.509 --> 01:34.844
-Why are you doing home?
-Oh!

01:36.096 --> 01:38.181
That working holiday thing
I told you about…

01:38.264 --> 01:40.642
-I wanna do one of those.
-Working holiday?

01:40.725 --> 01:42.852
-Yeah.
-So you can pick fruit in Australia?

01:42.936 --> 01:44.646
Australia? Why Australia?

01:44.729 --> 01:47.190
-Is the fruit good there?
-Not Australia. Canada.

01:47.273 --> 01:51.111
If you feel like picking fruit,
go over to your aunt's in Nonsan.

01:51.194 --> 01:52.070
Dad, fold some.

01:52.153 --> 01:54.823
-Oh, fine.
-Why go so far away just to do labor?

01:54.906 --> 01:56.658
-You don't have experience.
-I wanna try it.

01:56.741 --> 01:58.535
You sure you can? You should check.

01:58.618 --> 02:00.495
I wouldn't go right away.

02:00.578 --> 02:02.872
I'd need to get the visa
and prep for a while.

02:02.956 --> 02:06.209
Have to get a doctor's appointment
and all the paperwork. Everything I need.

02:06.292 --> 02:07.961
Wait. If you go to Australia…

02:08.044 --> 02:10.713
-So he can't use his savings account?
-Not Australia. Canada.

02:10.797 --> 02:13.133
-Do you have the money?
-Yeah, he still can.

02:13.216 --> 02:14.551
-I have savings?
-Can he?

02:14.634 --> 02:16.136
Hey, fold while you talk.

02:19.264 --> 02:22.433
Hey, loser.You give up already?

02:23.017 --> 02:24.561
Give up what, dumbass?

02:25.145 --> 02:27.355
Finding a job and a life, you broke ass.

02:28.398 --> 02:32.068
Oh, a job? Not really.
I haven't even really looked for one.

02:33.069 --> 02:36.030
And the trip? You still trying to escape?

02:38.032 --> 02:38.867
Hey.

02:39.492 --> 02:42.036
You… remember what high school was like?

02:43.496 --> 02:45.415
-Are you serious?
-Mm.

02:47.917 --> 02:49.419
Uh…

02:50.211 --> 02:51.379
I don't know.

02:52.589 --> 02:54.883
I remember the spaghetti was all right,
and…

02:55.383 --> 02:58.219
-And the school nurse was--
-You two never talk about high school.

02:58.970 --> 03:00.597
Were you guys actually close?

03:01.389 --> 03:03.308
We were trying to be considerate.

03:03.391 --> 03:06.019
We just didn't want you to feel left out,
all right?

03:06.102 --> 03:07.437
Oh, really?

03:09.522 --> 03:10.481
Why, what about it?

03:11.274 --> 03:12.233
Well,

03:13.067 --> 03:16.112
things have been smoother since then.

03:17.447 --> 03:20.158
I wanna live a different life
or something, I guess.

03:20.992 --> 03:24.662
Why isn't there anything
spec-- spectacular in our lives, man?

03:25.163 --> 03:28.416
Well, your life is pretty
spe-- spe-- spectacular, isn't it?

03:29.542 --> 03:30.418
Yeah?

03:31.002 --> 03:33.755
Hey. I've thought about this, okay?

03:34.255 --> 03:36.090
You're just gonna waste money again.

03:36.591 --> 03:40.053
Remember that gym membership
you had? You went only once, right?

03:40.136 --> 03:41.763
That was so freakin' stupid.

03:41.846 --> 03:45.433
Then, you spent 200,000 won
on that whole workout thing.

03:45.516 --> 03:47.977
Ah, shit, man. Pull-up bar.

03:48.061 --> 03:49.520
God, you're such an ass.

03:49.604 --> 03:52.357
And before that, what was it?

03:52.440 --> 03:56.194
You went and got all into board games
and spent all your time at the club. Like…

03:56.277 --> 03:58.446
Not like you didn't do
the same thing, asshole.

03:58.529 --> 04:00.198
Oppa. Check it out.

04:01.449 --> 04:03.493
"The night before last,
I had the hottest hook-up."

04:03.576 --> 04:05.119
Not that one, this one.

04:06.871 --> 04:09.082
"I'm a guy
who already did my military service."

04:09.165 --> 04:11.167
"I'm going back to school
after my working holiday."

04:11.251 --> 04:14.128
"All my friends have jobs now.
I don't know what I'm going to do."

04:14.212 --> 04:16.381
-"I'm so worried, so I'm writing this."
-Shit, man.

04:16.464 --> 04:18.424
-That's you!
-Go to hell.

04:18.508 --> 04:20.468
This is Tang in three years.

04:25.974 --> 04:28.434
This is Canada!

04:28.518 --> 04:30.395
It's the Rocky Mountains, everyone.

04:30.979 --> 04:32.355
Wow.

04:32.981 --> 04:34.691
Wow, it's really insane.

04:35.775 --> 04:37.694
You just have to come see this.

04:38.194 --> 04:40.571
Guys, it's totally awesome!

04:40.655 --> 04:42.532
Look at this amazing view!

04:42.615 --> 04:44.075
Making my way here was--

04:46.369 --> 04:47.745
Aah, shit.

04:49.580 --> 04:51.124
Give it a rest.

04:52.375 --> 04:53.543
…so hard.

04:54.669 --> 04:55.545
Guys.

04:56.129 --> 04:57.422
If heaven existed,

04:58.256 --> 04:59.882
this place would be it.

05:00.842 --> 05:03.428
STARTING APRIL 1
BEEF UP YOUR AVERAGE BODY!

05:09.517 --> 05:10.560
Shit.

05:26.034 --> 05:27.035
Hmm?

05:31.456 --> 05:34.125
YOUR ORDER HAS ARRIVED
ROCKY MOUNTAINS PICTURE FRAME NO.7

05:50.975 --> 05:52.143
Shit.

05:59.067 --> 06:00.443
Ah, shit.

06:05.114 --> 06:06.866
I want a refund.

06:07.617 --> 06:08.534
What?

06:09.077 --> 06:11.245
I said I want a refund.
I think it went bad.

06:14.540 --> 06:16.793
Well, it's not expired.

06:16.876 --> 06:19.712
If it isn't expired, then
you must have stored it wrong.

06:19.796 --> 06:21.923
It's the sanjeok. It tastes sour.

06:22.006 --> 06:24.008
Try it yourself if you don't believe me.

06:25.343 --> 06:28.346
That's… how it always tastes, so…

06:30.264 --> 06:31.265
Are you for real?

06:32.141 --> 06:33.935
What's your name? Jung Eun-seon?

06:34.018 --> 06:35.395
Hey!

06:35.478 --> 06:37.522
So? Am I the bad guy?

06:37.605 --> 06:38.815
Huh? Is that it?

06:38.898 --> 06:40.024
Hey, don't ignore me.

06:40.108 --> 06:42.610
-Wake up. Get your shit together.
-Here's your refund.

06:44.904 --> 06:45.863
You clean it up.

06:52.245 --> 06:54.622
Shouldn't you be here
before your shift starts?

07:16.978 --> 07:17.854
Huh.

07:21.065 --> 07:22.525
Now I'm swimming!

07:22.608 --> 07:26.362
-Oh, man! Let's try again.
-I'll get us another drink.

07:26.446 --> 07:27.822
No, buddy, that's okay.

07:27.905 --> 07:29.699
-This is the hotel…
-Seriously, let me.

07:29.782 --> 07:32.410
-Come on, man, it's my treat. No. Hey!
-Zip it, you. Enough!

07:32.493 --> 07:34.954
-I'm buying, ya bastard. You go sit.
-Yeah--

07:35.037 --> 07:36.497
-Go sit down.
-Hello.

07:36.581 --> 07:39.208
-All right, all right.
-Give me Esse.

07:42.753 --> 07:46.424
Hey, hey, no. I want the, uh, "Soon,"
with the bamboo on it.

07:46.924 --> 07:48.342
Oh, you mean Soo?

07:49.010 --> 07:49.927
These?

07:50.761 --> 07:53.431
Nah, not this one. The 0.5 milligram one.

08:01.772 --> 08:03.691
SMOKING CAN CAUSE ERECTILE DYSFUNCTION!

08:03.774 --> 08:06.235
Oh, fucking bitch. Not this…

08:07.278 --> 08:09.572
Get me one with another logo.

08:26.088 --> 08:28.508
There. One more.

08:29.675 --> 08:31.761
-Two packs cost 9,000.
-Hmm?

08:31.844 --> 08:33.304
9,000, please.

08:33.387 --> 08:36.224
Ah, shit, my… oh, money…

08:41.562 --> 08:45.441
I heard this is how kids these days
make a heart. Is that right?

08:45.525 --> 08:47.860
Not funny?

08:48.694 --> 08:51.322
God, you little shit… Here.

08:52.240 --> 08:55.535
Bring me a bottle of Cass
and dried squid legs outside, got it?

08:55.618 --> 08:56.702
-What?
-That's right.

08:56.786 --> 08:58.663
Sir, wait. You have to get it…

08:58.746 --> 08:59.622
Hey!

08:59.705 --> 09:02.458
Hey, let's have another round!

09:02.542 --> 09:04.043
Hey, why are your hands empty?

09:04.126 --> 09:06.337
-Just wait, you little bitch.
-Have a good day!

09:06.420 --> 09:10.174
-Hey, sir. I can't--
-Hey, do you have the squids I asked for?

09:10.258 --> 09:11.717
Not the dried ones.

09:11.801 --> 09:13.678
Listen. I can't bring them to you.

09:13.761 --> 09:15.429
-First, you have to pay.
-You fucker.

09:15.513 --> 09:18.516
-You think we're not gonna pay--
-Shit, man, stop. Knock it off!

09:18.599 --> 09:19.725
-I'm sorry.
-Yeah…

09:19.809 --> 09:22.436
-He's working. Why say that? Fucking hell.
-He's being a fucking ass.

09:22.520 --> 09:24.397
-"Fucking ass"? I'm sorry.
-Have a good day!

09:24.480 --> 09:28.776
He's not like that usually. I don't know
what his problem is. Oh, I'm sorry.

09:30.319 --> 09:34.949
Really, I mean it. He's normally
such a nice, courteous, and quiet guy.

09:35.032 --> 09:37.493
I don't know what's gotten into him.

09:38.202 --> 09:39.870
Yeah, he's not himself today.

09:39.954 --> 09:44.625
Thing is, he got an earful all day
from the site manager, that's why.

09:44.709 --> 09:46.419
-Ah, yeah…
-You got a plastic bag?

09:46.919 --> 09:49.463
-Yeah.
-Oh, wait a minute, yeah.

09:51.340 --> 09:52.341
Oh, gosh.

09:53.384 --> 09:57.305
You remind me of my kid back at the house,
having a tough time working and all.

09:57.388 --> 09:58.973
-Yeah.
-We'll be out of here soon.

09:59.056 --> 10:00.308
-Okay.
-How much is it?

10:00.391 --> 10:03.311
-15,150 won.
-Ten thousand…

10:03.394 --> 10:05.688
-And did you want a receipt?
-No. Thank you.

10:05.771 --> 10:08.691
-All right.
-Okay. 15,150 won.

10:08.774 --> 10:09.817
-Yeah.
-Have a good day!

10:09.900 --> 10:11.944
-Here's the 50.
-Hey! Get two more bottles.

10:12.028 --> 10:13.613
-Gosh.
-Sir, you can't smoke in here.

10:13.696 --> 10:15.114
-Oh, Lord.
-I can smoke, fuck it--

10:15.197 --> 10:17.074
-What makes you think you can smoke?
-Hey.

10:17.158 --> 10:18.159
Go on and get out.

10:18.242 --> 10:20.620
-Hey, did you pay?
-Oh, come on.

10:20.703 --> 10:22.913
-Let's go.
-Ugh, are you kidding me?

10:25.833 --> 10:28.461
-Hey, come on…
-Calm down. It's fine.

10:33.591 --> 10:34.967
BUTTER ROASTED

10:35.051 --> 10:36.469
Seriously?

10:37.720 --> 10:39.180
Spectacular, isn't it?

10:51.108 --> 10:52.360
Have a good day!

10:54.070 --> 10:55.321
Hey, Tang. Good work.

10:55.988 --> 10:57.031
-Go home now.
-Okay.

10:57.657 --> 10:59.450
Oh, sir.

10:59.950 --> 11:01.744
Could I borrow this hammer?

11:28.187 --> 11:29.146
Shit.

11:43.994 --> 11:44.870
Sir.

11:47.373 --> 11:48.916
Sir, you can't sleep there.

11:50.000 --> 11:51.043
Great.

12:04.265 --> 12:05.182
Uh, sir?

12:09.311 --> 12:10.438
Sir, wait.

12:11.564 --> 12:12.815
Hey, sir.

12:14.358 --> 12:15.192
Huh?

12:15.901 --> 12:19.155
Your, uh, buddy,
he's sleeping right over there.

12:20.364 --> 12:21.323
Oh?

12:21.866 --> 12:23.534
It's okay. Yeah.

12:24.118 --> 12:25.786
-Go. Go on.
-Huh?

12:26.370 --> 12:29.290
Uh, it's gonna start raining
pretty soon, so…

12:33.043 --> 12:34.253
Get outta here.

12:35.379 --> 12:36.505
Get lost.

13:00.154 --> 13:01.572
No, uh… I…

13:08.996 --> 13:12.500
You motherfucker.
Why, huh? You dumb son of a bitch!

13:12.583 --> 13:13.584
Why, huh?

13:14.126 --> 13:16.128
Why won't you go? You fucker!

13:16.212 --> 13:17.755
-I told you to go!
-Ah!

13:22.676 --> 13:25.429
-Gyeong-hwan. You motherfucker. Twerp.
-Son of a bitch.

13:25.513 --> 13:28.057
-You must have been hungry to cut in line?
-You pathetic dipshit.

13:28.140 --> 13:30.684
-Aren't you gonna help him?
-We were in front of you.

13:30.768 --> 13:32.603
-Are you gonna help?
-You're done for.

13:32.686 --> 13:34.647
-You son of a bitch.
-You gonna help?

13:34.730 --> 13:36.357
I bet he's full now.

13:36.440 --> 13:37.858
You fucking bastard.

13:37.942 --> 13:40.319
-Chin up, Gyeong-hwan.
-Hey, you're hurting him.

13:40.402 --> 13:43.906
Let's give him one good hit and end it.

13:43.989 --> 13:45.324
Just one. Hey, Tang.

13:45.407 --> 13:48.911
-I could use some more. Bastard.
-You pick. Number one, here…

13:48.994 --> 13:51.121
Two, right here…

13:51.205 --> 13:53.999
-Number three.
-Where could it be?

13:54.083 --> 13:55.751
-Oh, here. The balls.
-I'm good with that.

13:55.835 --> 13:57.461
-Pick one.
-Yeah.

13:57.545 --> 14:00.673
-Balls, good thinking.
-Choose already. Come on.

14:00.756 --> 14:02.883
-Hey, pick already!
-Gyeong-hwan.

14:02.967 --> 14:05.052
-You don't mind just having one ball?
-Can't decide?

14:05.135 --> 14:08.389
-Hey! Gyeong-hwan. Look at this bitch.
-Should I flick it? Kick it?

14:08.472 --> 14:10.850
-Fucking hell. You suck so much.
-Come on, man.

14:11.392 --> 14:12.852
The fuck, idiots? Are you both mute?

14:12.935 --> 14:14.645
-God, this is boring already.
-Bastards.

14:14.728 --> 14:16.814
-I feel so fucking bad for Gyeong-hwan.
-Fucker!

14:16.897 --> 14:18.148
-Hey!
-Boring.

14:18.232 --> 14:20.109
-This is no fun.
-Why won't you answer, bitch?

14:41.130 --> 14:42.590
Striking back

14:43.257 --> 14:45.175
has never been an option in my life.

14:48.846 --> 14:50.848
Life isn't an essay question.

14:52.057 --> 14:53.475
It's multiple choice.

14:55.603 --> 14:56.812
So, that day, why did I…

15:00.232 --> 15:02.359
Where on earth did I find the courage…

16:00.626 --> 16:03.128
Guys, if heaven existed,

16:03.712 --> 16:05.422
this place would be it.

16:29.989 --> 16:31.115
Oh.

16:35.869 --> 16:37.037
Uh, hey, sir?

16:38.622 --> 16:39.832
Oh…

16:46.338 --> 16:47.464
S-- sir?

16:47.965 --> 16:49.675
A-- are you okay?

16:49.758 --> 16:51.135
Are…

16:52.094 --> 16:53.095
Hey.

16:54.346 --> 16:55.723
Sir…

17:12.364 --> 17:13.574
S-- Hey, sir?

17:17.953 --> 17:18.787
Oh…

17:19.329 --> 17:20.789
S-- Hey, sir!

17:23.083 --> 17:25.294
Come on! Let's get another drink!

17:25.377 --> 17:26.420
Hold on!

17:26.503 --> 17:29.089
-Hey…
-It's pouring. Where would we go?

17:29.173 --> 17:30.883
This awesome pork skin place.

17:30.966 --> 17:33.385
Huh? Whatever, you can go alone.
I'm going home!

17:33.469 --> 17:36.513
Hey, come with me.
Come on, let's drink some more.

17:37.097 --> 17:38.974
Hey! Where are you going?

17:41.477 --> 17:42.478
Huh?

17:43.187 --> 17:44.980
Rex.

17:46.648 --> 17:47.775
What is it?

17:48.984 --> 17:50.110
We gotta go.

17:50.694 --> 17:51.695
Yeah.

17:52.362 --> 17:53.447
Let's go.

17:57.242 --> 17:59.411
Why is there music coming from the ground?

18:00.454 --> 18:02.456
This song is so old.

18:13.217 --> 18:15.094
Hmm. Rex.

18:15.969 --> 18:18.430
Hey, come back.
You're going the wrong way.

18:18.514 --> 18:19.556
SEEING-EYE DOG

18:19.640 --> 18:20.516
Rex!

18:20.599 --> 18:22.935
Come on, what are you doing?

18:24.186 --> 18:25.270
Rex.

18:25.354 --> 18:27.815
Oh, what are you doing, huh? Let's go!

18:30.943 --> 18:33.612
Okay, buddy. All right, let's go. Come on.

19:17.656 --> 19:19.575
Do you feel wronged?

19:20.075 --> 19:21.118
Do you?

19:24.913 --> 19:25.956
Jeez.

19:27.791 --> 19:29.084
Hey, part-timer.

19:30.335 --> 19:32.963
You do a terrible thing
like this to someone,

19:33.630 --> 19:35.966
and you're only worried about yourself.

19:37.217 --> 19:39.094
How do you sleep at night?

19:41.013 --> 19:41.972
Look…

19:43.307 --> 19:44.433
I have

19:45.767 --> 19:46.977
an old mother.

19:47.603 --> 19:49.062
She has dementia.

19:50.772 --> 19:51.732
You know what else?

19:52.399 --> 19:53.859
I have three kids.

19:54.484 --> 19:56.361
You see, my kids…

19:56.445 --> 19:59.114
They're what get me
through the day.

20:00.365 --> 20:01.783
What are you gonna do?

20:02.367 --> 20:03.327
Huh?

20:03.994 --> 20:06.788
'Cause this is all your fault, you know?

20:07.748 --> 20:08.707
Hey, buddy…

20:10.167 --> 20:13.128
What did I say? Huh?

20:13.212 --> 20:18.091
I only just wanted you to leave me alone.

20:18.175 --> 20:19.176
You fucker!

20:59.716 --> 21:01.176
Open the door.

21:02.052 --> 21:03.637
It's Gyeong-hwan.

21:06.306 --> 21:08.433
Dude, open the door. Please.

21:09.685 --> 21:10.894
Hey, thank you. Thanks.

21:11.436 --> 21:13.355
Why didn't you answer my calls, jerk?

21:13.981 --> 21:15.023
Oh, I'm dying.

21:15.565 --> 21:17.859
Hey, could you get me
a cup of water, please?

21:18.652 --> 21:21.071
I got shitfaced
with the guys that I play with.

21:21.822 --> 21:24.032
I, of course,
outdrank all of them, though.

21:26.827 --> 21:29.621
Oh, I told Mi-yeong
I was drinking with you,

21:29.705 --> 21:31.915
and so you gotta back me up, okay?

21:32.874 --> 21:36.545
DOES YOUR SENTENCE GET REDUCED
IF YOU KILLED SOMEONE BY ACCIDENT?

21:55.188 --> 21:57.149
No way. I didn't…

21:57.232 --> 21:59.192
You've got the wrong guy!

21:59.276 --> 22:01.111
-He's in there!
-Back off! Back off!

22:01.194 --> 22:05.532
I'm telling you, I'm innocent!
You can't do this! Let me go!

22:06.950 --> 22:09.369
Hey, are you asleep?

22:13.582 --> 22:15.167
Gi-hun and his gang.

22:17.836 --> 22:19.796
What do you imagine they're doin' now?

22:24.259 --> 22:25.594
Ah, fuck.

22:27.054 --> 22:30.891
They must still be a bunch of shithead,
lowlife idiots making trouble, right?

22:34.311 --> 22:35.187
Fuck me.

22:35.270 --> 22:36.646
No.

22:36.730 --> 22:38.815
They're doin' fuckin' well.

22:41.443 --> 22:43.570
I looked them up on Instagram.

22:45.906 --> 22:48.909
That asshole Gi-hun has his own business.

22:50.035 --> 22:52.954
He's always bragging
about his Mercedes online.

22:53.580 --> 22:55.707
One's a seventh-grade teacher.

22:56.792 --> 22:58.377
One just got married.

22:59.961 --> 23:02.214
They're all doin' fuckin' great.

23:02.297 --> 23:03.673
Livin' large.

23:05.384 --> 23:07.594
What are you doing?

23:08.261 --> 23:09.137
Huh?

23:10.180 --> 23:12.015
I said, what are you looking for?

23:12.849 --> 23:13.975
Oh.

23:14.059 --> 23:15.435
My promise ring.

23:16.353 --> 23:17.521
Promise ring?

23:18.605 --> 23:19.940
What's it look like?

23:20.023 --> 23:22.901
It was the same when I cheated
with a girl from the board game club

23:22.984 --> 23:24.111
before my service.

23:24.194 --> 23:25.070
Huh…

23:25.153 --> 23:27.906
I was gonna break up
with my girlfriend if I got caught.

23:28.615 --> 23:29.741
Keep lookin'.

23:31.868 --> 23:34.037
But luckily, that never happened.

23:37.374 --> 23:38.250
There.

23:44.840 --> 23:45.882
What are you doing?

23:47.509 --> 23:49.594
Oh, shoot. My tablet.

23:50.804 --> 23:52.431
-Oh, that?
-Yeah.

23:53.348 --> 23:56.393
-Hey, let's all go with Ji-eun.
-You asshole…

23:56.476 --> 23:57.561
Shit…

23:57.644 --> 23:59.229
-What?
-Motherfuckers.

23:59.312 --> 24:02.190
What? Why not, man?

24:03.733 --> 24:06.403
And when I stole something
back in high school,

24:06.486 --> 24:08.780
I got lucky and got away with it too.

24:08.864 --> 24:11.575
Hey, you had it with you
at lunch, didn't you?

24:17.205 --> 24:18.832
No one suspected me.

24:21.209 --> 24:22.502
It felt like

24:23.211 --> 24:24.921
everything was going my way.

24:35.640 --> 24:36.558
Hey.

24:38.852 --> 24:40.395
What…

24:40.479 --> 24:42.230
What time did you get here earlier?

24:44.274 --> 24:45.484
Eleven.

24:47.694 --> 24:48.945
No, idiot.

24:50.280 --> 24:52.824
You got here when I got home from work.
That's ten.

24:53.700 --> 24:55.911
Oh, yeah, ten.
Right.

25:00.415 --> 25:01.333
No.

25:01.917 --> 25:06.046
I watched the soccer game
till the end, so it was 11. You dumbass.

25:15.055 --> 25:16.806
When you go on your trip,

25:17.432 --> 25:19.476
can you give me the pull-up bar?

25:20.852 --> 25:21.853
Oh, shit.

25:24.314 --> 25:26.483
Just go to sleep, you freeloading idiot.

25:27.275 --> 25:29.653
Stop talking to me so I can.

25:29.736 --> 25:32.280
I have a morning class tomorrow.

25:59.975 --> 26:01.351
Ah, shit.

26:16.199 --> 26:17.742
-Yong-jae.
-Yes, sir!

26:20.620 --> 26:22.080
Did you find anything there?

26:22.163 --> 26:25.292
Uh, there's a security camera
in that alley over by the market,

26:25.375 --> 26:26.334
but nothing here.

26:26.418 --> 26:29.337
This place has been empty
'cause of the redevelopment project.

26:29.421 --> 26:31.590
-Nothin's here.
-Hey, over there. That house.

26:31.673 --> 26:34.843
-Does anyone live there?
-The one up there? I'll check.

26:34.926 --> 26:37.137
-Ask the patrol unit.
-Hurry up. Go on.

26:37.220 --> 26:39.097
-I'll go check.
-Ah, Christ.

26:39.180 --> 26:41.391
Hey, hey, hey.
Tell him to put his gloves on.

26:41.474 --> 26:42.684
You too, come on.

26:42.767 --> 26:46.354
I'm not doing anything.
Put your gloves on, Detective Jang.

26:47.439 --> 26:48.440
Come on.

26:49.232 --> 26:50.859
God, you never listen.

26:55.655 --> 26:57.532
Hey, why aren't you turning that off?

26:58.074 --> 26:59.075
Where is it?

27:00.952 --> 27:02.621
What's wrong with this?

27:03.788 --> 27:05.790
Fuck, I'm late!

27:07.542 --> 27:09.336
Oh, my head's pounding.

27:10.086 --> 27:12.964
Oh shit. I'm late,
I'm late, I'm late, I'm late.

27:13.632 --> 27:14.549
I'm outta here.

27:14.633 --> 27:16.301
Shit, I'm so late.

27:16.801 --> 27:18.053
Oh crap!

27:18.928 --> 27:21.556
My day shift girl says she's sick
and can't make it.

27:21.640 --> 27:23.600
But honestly, I bet she isn't really.

27:23.683 --> 27:25.518
Probably has a date with her boyfriend.

27:25.602 --> 27:26.436
BOSS

27:26.519 --> 27:28.730
But what can you do? She says she's sick.

27:29.314 --> 27:31.608
You can fill in for her, right?

27:33.109 --> 27:35.528
Get here as soon as you can, okay?

27:36.196 --> 27:37.614
I'll fill in until then.

27:38.323 --> 27:40.659
Ugh, I stayed up all night. I'm so tired.

28:03.348 --> 28:04.516
-Yes.
-Have a good day!

28:04.599 --> 28:07.560
Two people, dead on the ground,
right near the market,

28:07.644 --> 28:09.020
It's unbelievable!

28:09.104 --> 28:10.021
Hello.

28:10.897 --> 28:13.483
They need to clean up these streets.
What kind of country is this?

28:13.566 --> 28:15.276
The police just sit on their asses.

28:15.360 --> 28:17.779
I've never seen a patrol car
in this neighborhood.

28:19.114 --> 28:20.532
Need cigarettes?

28:20.615 --> 28:22.283
How many, uh…

28:22.367 --> 28:24.327
security cameras does this place have?

28:24.994 --> 28:25.870
What?

28:33.420 --> 28:36.923
-Her face is fucking…
-What about her?

28:37.006 --> 28:39.217
She keeps giving me
a bunch of shit.

28:39.300 --> 28:41.136
I fucking hate her, seriously, bro.

28:42.178 --> 28:44.806
-Wait, who are you talking about?
-You know.

28:44.889 --> 28:47.225
That bitch that smells
like fabric softener.

28:47.308 --> 28:49.561
I don't know what the teachers look like.

28:49.644 --> 28:51.771
Dumbass.
Come to school for once in your life.

28:51.855 --> 28:53.732
Let me get a light.

28:55.150 --> 28:58.862
Hey, sir. Excuse me,
but could I borrow, um, your lighter?

29:01.573 --> 29:02.949
I don't smoke, punk.

29:03.658 --> 29:05.118
Ah. Thanks anyway.

29:07.537 --> 29:09.456
Man…

29:09.539 --> 29:10.790
What? What's up?

29:12.083 --> 29:14.043
-Hey, so… I'm a punk?
-Hey, hey, hey.

29:14.127 --> 29:15.545
-Let's go. I've got a vape.
-Get off.

29:15.628 --> 29:16.921
-Let's smoke this.
-Let go of me.

29:17.005 --> 29:18.423
-You look familiar.
-Come on.

29:18.506 --> 29:20.175
-Come on, Jae-jun.
-Oh yeah? That so?

29:20.258 --> 29:22.802
-Let's go, you idiot.
-Wanna go to the station now?

29:22.886 --> 29:25.930
-Mm-hmm. You get all the hard drives?
-Yes, sir. I got everything.

29:26.014 --> 29:28.141
-Let's go!
-Oh, and put these boys in the car.

29:28.224 --> 29:29.934
-Wait.
-They need a lesson.

29:30.018 --> 29:33.146
-What?
-Wait, we aren't high school students.

29:33.229 --> 29:35.064
-We're not.
-Get in the black car now.

29:35.148 --> 29:36.733
-We're not in high school.
-Uh-huh…

29:36.816 --> 29:38.067
-Right,
-Really, sir…

29:38.151 --> 29:40.111
-Yeah, sure, sure.
-We aren't… Sir, listen.

29:40.195 --> 29:42.071
-We're 20, sir.
-Seriously, bro…

29:42.155 --> 29:43.907
You idiots. God.

29:43.990 --> 29:45.909
What is it this time?

29:45.992 --> 29:48.620
-I swear, this time we didn't do it.
-As if.

29:49.579 --> 29:51.247
-Look at this haircut.
-Don't touch my hair.

29:51.331 --> 29:53.458
-What did they do wrong?
-But we weren't…

29:53.541 --> 29:55.919
They're just petty offenders.

29:57.045 --> 29:58.630
Look at you idiots.

29:58.713 --> 30:02.425
Hey, he's just raggin' on you 'cause
you guys are slouchin' in your chairs.

30:03.259 --> 30:07.096
See, there's not a lot
I can do about you boys.

30:08.932 --> 30:10.391
I'm givin' you a warning.

30:10.975 --> 30:16.523
But… kids need consequences
to put some sense into your heads.

30:16.606 --> 30:18.608
Whether it's a fine or some jail time.

30:19.901 --> 30:24.322
-Right, Detective Jang?
-If I catch you guys at it one more time…

30:24.405 --> 30:25.281
Hmm?

30:25.365 --> 30:26.449
You heard him.

30:27.242 --> 30:29.494
-Sit up straight.
-Did you get anything from the cameras?

30:29.577 --> 30:31.579
-Not really.
-Want me to call your parents?

30:31.663 --> 30:34.582
I'm checking out some people
the shop owners might've run into.

30:35.124 --> 30:37.877
How could they both end up
dying after a fight, though?

30:38.545 --> 30:40.380
The bodies are in
completely different areas.

30:40.463 --> 30:41.464
Yes, that's true.

30:41.548 --> 30:46.010
Hey, but when your brain hemorrhages,
you don't go down right on the spot.

30:46.553 --> 30:49.430
It's possible you kill the other guy,
then collapse and die on the way.

30:49.514 --> 30:50.765
That's true too.

30:50.849 --> 30:53.518
You just have to go
off of the test results we get.

30:53.601 --> 30:56.104
You can't rely
on your gut feeling with this.

30:56.187 --> 30:59.065
-Just believe what you see, all right?
-Well, I'm lookin'.

31:00.024 --> 31:02.443
Fine. He won't listen.

31:02.527 --> 31:04.195
Do you wanna turn out like him?

31:04.279 --> 31:05.947
Why are your pants all ripped up?

31:06.447 --> 31:08.908
You'll freeze to death
trying to look cool, dummy.

31:14.914 --> 31:16.708
The guy who worked here yesterday.

31:17.667 --> 31:18.501
Yesterday?

31:19.168 --> 31:20.003
Yeah.

31:20.587 --> 31:23.548
The one who came in at 4:00 p.m.
and left at 10:00 in the evening.

31:23.631 --> 31:27.135
Oh! You must be talking about Tang.
Lee Tang.

31:28.803 --> 31:30.138
His name is Lee Tang?

31:30.805 --> 31:32.640
Lee Tang. Yes. The name's odd.

31:32.724 --> 31:36.060
-Can you give me his contact information?
-Right, his number.

31:36.144 --> 31:37.103
Uh… Oh.

31:37.186 --> 31:38.938
Ah! There he is.

31:39.689 --> 31:42.442
-Hey, just in time, Tang. Come on in.
-Have a good day!

31:42.525 --> 31:44.068
You heard what happened yesterday?

31:44.152 --> 31:45.612
-Huh?
-There was a murder.

31:45.695 --> 31:47.196
There's a detective here now.

31:47.280 --> 31:50.033
So, uh, go talk to him.
Tell him everything you know.

31:50.116 --> 31:51.326
Have a good day!

31:53.119 --> 31:54.162
Have a seat.

32:00.752 --> 32:01.669
Oh.

32:05.590 --> 32:07.550
I haven't been sleepin' well lately.

32:10.678 --> 32:13.598
So, if you're a college student,
I guess you're at Usang?

32:15.642 --> 32:16.768
-Yeah.
-Mm.

32:20.313 --> 32:21.564
So…

32:24.609 --> 32:26.402
Are we gonna talk right here?

32:29.238 --> 32:30.740
You want to go to the station?

32:31.866 --> 32:33.159
Oh. No.

32:36.663 --> 32:38.498
You recall those older guys, yeah?

32:38.581 --> 32:40.750
This guy? Hmm?

32:45.463 --> 32:46.589
They threw money

32:48.675 --> 32:50.385
and made you bring food out.

32:51.344 --> 32:52.470
And left a mess.

32:53.054 --> 32:54.555
They were pretty drunk.

32:56.557 --> 32:57.809
That why you killed them?

32:57.892 --> 32:59.519
Huh?

33:05.608 --> 33:08.736
I'm screwin' around.
You really seem nervous.

33:13.992 --> 33:18.955
Those two drank here at this table
for somethin' like two hours yesterday.

33:20.164 --> 33:22.125
I need to know what they talked about.

33:22.959 --> 33:25.878
It was late at night, so I'm guessing
you could hear 'em from inside.

33:26.462 --> 33:27.922
So, do you remember anything?

33:29.882 --> 33:30.925
Just…

33:33.136 --> 33:34.679
a bit about their family.

33:36.264 --> 33:37.223
Family?

33:38.141 --> 33:39.851
How things have been hard.

33:40.810 --> 33:44.605
-I told you my mother has dementia, okay?
-That his mother has dementia.

33:44.689 --> 33:46.065
Besides, I've got three children!

33:46.149 --> 33:47.859
And that he has three kids.

33:48.776 --> 33:50.528
And then what?

33:51.070 --> 33:52.488
AN YONG-JAE

34:37.366 --> 34:38.701
I… I'm not really…

34:38.785 --> 34:40.078
Detective Jang.

34:40.161 --> 34:42.163
They identified the prints. It's a match.

34:43.081 --> 34:44.791
It's like Detective Park said.

34:44.874 --> 34:47.418
They killed each other.
We found a witness too.

34:48.002 --> 34:49.253
His statement even matches.

34:49.337 --> 34:51.589
Apparently, the two got drunk
and got into an argument.

34:51.672 --> 34:54.008
Lee Gwang-hun must've hit him
with a brick first.

34:54.759 --> 34:56.844
We found blood from Lee Gwang-hun's head.

34:57.428 --> 34:59.138
It was on Kim Myeong-jin's speaker.

34:59.222 --> 35:02.225
It looks like…
they did actually kill each other.

35:03.309 --> 35:04.393
Mm. Mm.

35:16.197 --> 35:17.907
Could I borrow this hammer?

35:34.132 --> 35:35.883
-Yong-jae.
-Sir?

35:38.344 --> 35:39.387
Well done.

35:42.140 --> 35:44.559
You found the witness too. That's good.

35:45.143 --> 35:46.769
I appreciate it.

35:48.104 --> 35:50.565
You did good, but be careful.

35:51.774 --> 35:52.775
About what?

35:52.859 --> 35:55.111
You talked about the case
in front of the kid.

35:56.988 --> 35:58.322
Don't get sloppy.

36:03.744 --> 36:05.204
That was neglectful.

36:05.705 --> 36:07.165
Sorry if I made you Jang-gry.

36:10.251 --> 36:12.295
Oh. No, I was joking.

36:18.885 --> 36:22.013
They choose to fight somewhere
there aren't any security cameras.

36:22.096 --> 36:23.306
What are the odds?

36:23.389 --> 36:25.266
I mean, it's unbelievable.

36:26.350 --> 36:29.478
So he got hit there, then walked all
the way over here before he dropped dead?

36:29.562 --> 36:31.647
-How's that even possible?
-Whatever.

36:31.731 --> 36:33.691
Hey, hand me the wire stripper.

36:33.774 --> 36:34.609
Okay.

36:35.318 --> 36:36.194
Here.

36:36.277 --> 36:38.696
The man's eyes were swollen too.

36:38.779 --> 36:42.408
Which means he would have manifested
these symptoms after the first blow.

36:43.284 --> 36:48.039
However, the autopsy shows
a blood alcohol level of 0.13,

36:48.122 --> 36:50.666
so there's a chance
he might not have felt them at all.

36:53.878 --> 36:56.047
How long have you known
Mr. Kim Myeong-jin?

36:59.634 --> 37:03.179
I think I've known him
for around maybe three years or so.

37:03.763 --> 37:06.224
I'm home! I brought over a friend.

37:06.307 --> 37:08.309
-You don't mind, right?
-The kids are sleeping! Sh!

37:08.392 --> 37:11.145
-Sh! All right. Get us a drink and food.
-Oh, ma'am, excuse me.

37:11.229 --> 37:13.689
-One day, my husband…
-He said we could come here.

37:13.773 --> 37:15.399
-He brought him home.
-What'd I tell ya?

37:15.483 --> 37:17.318
Said he was a friend who worked with him.

37:17.401 --> 37:18.527
…real big heart.

37:18.611 --> 37:19.862
I'm heading out.

37:19.946 --> 37:22.448
-Hey! Hey, Yong-jun.
-All right, see you.

37:22.531 --> 37:24.909
-He was a caring man.
-Wait. Hang on.

37:24.992 --> 37:26.911
-Always very nice.
-I have something for you.

37:26.994 --> 37:30.331
-I know it's not much, but take it.
-Ah, you don't need to do that.

37:30.414 --> 37:31.499
-Oh, Myeong-jin!
-Bye, kiddo.

37:31.582 --> 37:34.001
Keep doing that,
and you're gonna spoil the kid.

37:34.085 --> 37:35.711
-Oh, come on.
-See ya.

37:35.795 --> 37:38.130
All right. Bye.

37:38.214 --> 37:40.299
-He became friends with the kids too.
-Come on.

37:40.383 --> 37:42.093
And would give them pocket money.

37:42.843 --> 37:46.514
He'd even remember my birthday,
and my husband never did.

37:46.597 --> 37:51.102
Wow, your cooking is just as good
as a professional chef!

37:51.602 --> 37:54.397
Mm! God, your skills are wasted
as a housewife.

37:55.106 --> 37:56.482
Man!

37:59.151 --> 38:01.320
-Ma'am.
-Yes?

38:01.404 --> 38:03.572
Would you like
to come have a drink?

38:30.891 --> 38:32.143
So…

38:32.226 --> 38:35.896
You were going to get a divorce,
as soon as your son moved out,

38:35.980 --> 38:38.941
and marry your husband's friend
after that.

38:40.109 --> 38:41.402
Does that sound right?

38:44.447 --> 38:45.323
Yes.

38:45.406 --> 38:46.657
Potato, potah-to.

38:47.491 --> 38:50.953
What's the point of marriage
if you just let yourself be seduced, huh?

38:51.495 --> 38:54.874
And she's serving food at her lover's
funeral when her husband also died?

38:54.957 --> 38:56.000
She's nuts!

38:56.083 --> 38:56.917
Hey.

38:58.044 --> 38:59.170
See, look.

39:01.505 --> 39:03.758
That's no way to behave
when you've got a son that age.

39:03.841 --> 39:05.343
Even I'd knife the guy.

39:05.426 --> 39:08.137
-Not a knife. A brick.
-Oh yeah? So?

39:08.220 --> 39:10.931
We didn't find any blood on the brick.
What's that about?

39:11.015 --> 39:13.476
-Don't start with that.
-And about Kim Myeong-jin.

39:14.226 --> 39:17.480
-There's somethin' strange about him.
-What are you sayin'?

39:17.563 --> 39:19.774
I looked up his records,
but nothing came up.

39:19.857 --> 39:22.902
And, most importantly, I think, well…

39:22.985 --> 39:24.445
I think I've seen the guy.

39:24.528 --> 39:27.948
Doesn't work if you think you've seen him.
Just believe what you see.

39:30.326 --> 39:32.912
Enjoy your break.
I gotta go somewhere.

39:32.995 --> 39:33.996
I'll come with you.

39:46.801 --> 39:48.344
Can you recommend a gum?

39:49.095 --> 39:50.262
OH YEAH!
BUBBLE GUM

39:50.346 --> 39:51.806
Is this bubble gum?

39:52.390 --> 39:55.017
Yeah. I saw you blowing a bubble before.

39:57.686 --> 40:00.898
I can do that
with regular chewing gum as well.

40:02.775 --> 40:03.692
Oh.

40:04.276 --> 40:05.319
So what? Huh?

40:09.198 --> 40:13.160
You think that…
bubble gum and chewing gum are different?

40:15.955 --> 40:18.916
You keep chewing,
and you just blow bubbles all the same.

40:22.420 --> 40:23.629
How do I say it?

40:26.424 --> 40:29.969
Murder's just like that too.
It just happens.

40:34.723 --> 40:36.559
You're not a witness, although…

40:37.143 --> 40:40.062
when people are the last
to see a murder victim before they die,

40:40.146 --> 40:42.815
they tend to suffer
from trauma afterwards.

40:42.898 --> 40:45.693
I thought I might have
scared you too much earlier.

40:47.862 --> 40:51.532
And judging by your looks
and your name, I get a feeling

40:52.241 --> 40:55.578
that you might have it a bit rough
in life in general, and…

40:56.495 --> 40:58.456
let me just say, I can sympathize.

40:59.290 --> 41:00.207
Hmm?

41:00.291 --> 41:02.668
JANG NAN-GAM
NATIONAL POLICE AGENCY

41:05.421 --> 41:07.923
I became a cop
so people wouldn't think I'm a joke.

41:08.966 --> 41:10.176
You get it, right?

41:14.430 --> 41:15.389
Take care.

41:15.890 --> 41:17.057
Thanks. Come again.

41:17.141 --> 41:18.517
No, thanks.

41:19.310 --> 41:20.853
You won't be seeing me again.

41:36.285 --> 41:38.913
-Have a good day!
-Well, would you look at that?

41:39.663 --> 41:41.123
You little fucking punk.

41:42.041 --> 41:43.417
What are you doing here?

41:44.251 --> 41:45.503
So, what's your deal?

41:45.586 --> 41:48.214
You didn't answer my calls or texts.

41:48.297 --> 41:51.550
Oh, I didn't tell you? My phone broke.

41:51.634 --> 41:54.970
So then why haven't you had it fixed?
God.

41:55.054 --> 41:57.181
Why aren't you going to school?

41:58.933 --> 42:00.851
I have a family thing.

42:02.811 --> 42:06.148
Hey… I heard some guys got killed
near here, bro.

42:06.732 --> 42:08.651
Wanna hear something really funny?

42:08.734 --> 42:12.947
Yesterday, after class,
a detective came to see me and Mi-yeong.

42:13.030 --> 42:15.241
He was asking us a bunch of stuff.

42:15.324 --> 42:17.660
He wanted to know
what you were up to that day.

42:17.743 --> 42:19.328
It was intense as hell.

42:19.912 --> 42:22.873
And it was almost
like he thought you were the murderer.

42:22.957 --> 42:24.500
A professor walked by,

42:24.583 --> 42:26.544
and he was totally staring at us.

42:26.627 --> 42:29.255
I can't seem
to get drunk these days.

42:30.172 --> 42:31.757
What is this, water?

42:32.299 --> 42:34.343
Let's do another round.

42:34.885 --> 42:38.430
It's been so hard to get drunk.
Like, especially today, even. Shit.

42:39.807 --> 42:43.811
I drank with the guys a while back,
and I freaking destroyed them.

42:43.894 --> 42:45.479
Drank, like, ten bottles.

42:46.188 --> 42:47.523
Mm. Yeah, go ahead.

42:59.034 --> 43:00.911
Detective Jang! Detective Jang!

43:07.543 --> 43:08.877
Breaking news.

43:09.461 --> 43:13.507
In regards to the murder in an alley
in Yuseong-gu, Daejeon, a few days ago,

43:14.008 --> 43:18.304
an investigation into the identity
of Mr. Kim, a victim of the case,

43:18.387 --> 43:20.306
revealed him to be Kim Myeong-jin,

43:20.389 --> 43:22.683
a construction worker
who lived in the area.

43:23.267 --> 43:25.894
A closer analysis of his DNA revealed…

43:26.395 --> 43:28.981
-Kim Myeong-jin, who you said felt off?
-Yeah.

43:29.064 --> 43:32.568
His age, history,
none of it was real.

43:32.651 --> 43:34.278
I ran a background check,

43:34.361 --> 43:36.655
and this man, it turns out, is Yeo Bu-il.

43:37.615 --> 43:39.867
It was actually a match
for that of Mr. Yeo,

43:39.950 --> 43:44.413
the suspect in a serial murder
that took place in Gangwon-do in 2009.

43:46.290 --> 43:48.125
The police found Kim's true identity

43:48.208 --> 43:50.961
after they conducted
a more detailed DNA analysis

43:51.045 --> 43:53.213
following suspicions about his records.

43:53.297 --> 43:57.343
The discovery that Kim's DNA matched
that of the serial murder suspect, Yeo,

43:57.426 --> 44:00.638
and the fact that he had been living
under an alias all this time

44:00.721 --> 44:02.681
comes as a shock to many.

44:03.349 --> 44:04.975
Oh, oh, Yeo Bu-il!

44:05.059 --> 44:07.770
-Ah!
-I wasn't sure either.

44:08.354 --> 44:10.481
Then I recognized him right away
when I saw the picture.

44:10.564 --> 44:12.483
WANTED FOR MURDER
NAME: YEO BU-IL

44:12.566 --> 44:14.735
One of the characteristics of a psychopath

44:14.818 --> 44:19.573
is that they are experts when it comes
to manipulation, deception, and disguises.

44:22.576 --> 44:24.828
Jesus, isn't it strange, huh?

44:25.329 --> 44:27.706
It's like they say. What is it?

44:27.790 --> 44:29.750
-Uh… comeuppance.
-Yeah…

44:29.833 --> 44:31.752
He got what was comin' to him.

44:31.835 --> 44:33.921
The discovery
that Kim was actually Yeo,

44:34.004 --> 44:36.382
the suspect for the serial murder
in Gangwon-do,

44:36.465 --> 44:39.718
has led to renewed attention
on the vicious crimes years ago.

44:39.802 --> 44:43.681
He broke into a house for the insurance
payout and murdered the entire family…

45:04.201 --> 45:06.120
You servicing yourself

45:06.662 --> 45:08.288
'cause you killed a bad man?

45:11.875 --> 45:12.960
Hey, part-timer.

45:13.043 --> 45:15.379
The heart is

45:16.004 --> 45:19.341
so very cunning, isn't it?

45:23.345 --> 45:25.305
You murdered a family
for the insurance money.

45:26.473 --> 45:29.351
Hid in a mountain, then raped and killed
college kids who went for a hike

45:29.435 --> 45:30.978
before dumping their bodies.

45:31.895 --> 45:33.731
And you say what?

45:44.867 --> 45:47.745
I have an old mother at home.

45:48.245 --> 45:49.079
And…

45:49.163 --> 45:52.332
And I also have three kids.

45:52.416 --> 45:55.544
I heard you went from place to place,
killing a fuckload of people.

45:57.087 --> 45:59.298
Right up until you died in my hands!

46:01.675 --> 46:04.428
There's a lot more that aren't
on the internet and news, aren't there?

46:04.511 --> 46:06.847
And you say what?

46:06.930 --> 46:09.266
The stuff about your mother
and kids was all bullshit!

46:09.349 --> 46:11.810
They were all lies, weren't they? Huh?

47:17.960 --> 47:19.086
Ooh!

47:19.169 --> 47:21.213
There you go. Good job!

47:21.296 --> 47:24.049
Good boy. Yeah.

47:24.132 --> 47:26.093
Well done! Good!

47:26.176 --> 47:28.095
One more time? Okay?

47:28.178 --> 47:29.638
Here we go!

47:32.808 --> 47:35.769
There you go. Good job!

47:36.687 --> 47:38.981
One more. Go.
